CLIFF 1.1
namespace: clarion
clan: lit-modern
source-language: en-US
target-language: zh-CN
title: "Modern literary stratum - narration, dialogue, monologue, description"
info: "Original modern literary English composed for CLARION, rendered into literary Chinese that preserves voice, rhythm, point of view and the recurring wind-bell motif."
standard: "Preserve each character's voice and the narrator's point of view. Localize idioms rather than translating them literally. Render the recurring motif consistently. Dialogue must read as natural spoken Chinese, not stiff written prose."

[narration]
type: narration
context: "A long narrative paragraph that opens a fictional harbour-town story and introduces the recurring wind-bell motif."

<narration-open>
source: "The town had kept its old manners longer than it kept its money. At the end of every workday Maren walked the harbour road the way a clock walks its dial, and each evening the last thing she heard before the dark came down was the tin wind-bell over the chandler's door, telling the street that the tide had turned and that the world, for a little while, would go on without her. She did not hurry. The salt worked its way into everything she owned, and she had stopped minding it years ago."
target: "这座镇子把旧日的规矩留得比钱更久。每个收工后的黄昏，玛伦都像钟走表盘一样沿着码头路走上一遍；而每个傍晚，天黑下来之前，她最后听见的，总是杂货铺门楣上那串锡风铃，向整条街报信：潮水已经转了向，世界暂时不再需要她。她不赶路。盐渗进了她所有的家当，她多年前就不再计较。"
status: final
emotion: [nostalgic, calm]

<narration-memory>
source: "Of all the things the town let slip into the sea, the sound of that bell was the one thing it kept onshore. Men forgot their own birthdays and the names of ships they had crewed, but every one of them could tell you what the wind was doing the last time the bell rang plain."
target: "这座镇子把许多东西都放进了海里，唯独那铃的声音，它留在了岸上。有人忘记自己的生日，忘记自己当年跑过哪条船，可谁都说得清，上一次那铃清清亮亮响起时，风在往哪边吹。"
status: final
emotion: [nostalgic, calm]

[dialogue]
type: dialogue
context: "An exchange at the harbour wall between Maren and the taciturn ferryman Sol; the two voices must stay distinct."

<dialogue-wall>
source: "\"Wind's back,\" said Sol. \"Didn't figure you'd be out.\" \"I couldn't sleep,\" Maren said. \"The bell again?\" \"The bell.\" Sol folded his arms. \"Folks round here reckon a wind-bell don't ring for the wind. It rings for what the wind forgot.\" \"That's the whole of it,\" Maren said. \"You sleep any better for knowing?\" \"I know the letter F in better, and that's the whole of it,\" said Sol."
target: "「起风了。」索尔说，「没想到你还会出来。」「睡不着。」玛伦说。「又是那铃？」「是那铃。」索尔抱起双臂：「这一带的人都说，风铃不为风响，是为风忘了的事响。」「就是这么回事。」玛伦说。「知道了，就能睡得好些吗？」「我知道『好』这个字的写法，也就知道这么回事。」索尔说。"
status: final
emotion: [calm, serious]

<dialogue-breakfast>
source: "\"You'd keep the bell if the sea gave it back,\" Sol said one morning. \"Wouldn't you?\" \"I'd hang it where it hangs now,\" Maren said. \"Then what's all the listening for?\" \"To be sure it's still there.\" Sol shook his head. \"It'll be there after both of us,\" he said, \"and it won't miss us.\" \"I know.\" \"Then you know more than most.\" \"I know the listening, anyway.\" \"That's not the same thing.\" \"It's close enough,\" Maren said. \"It's close enough for me.\""
target: "「要是海把铃还回来，你会留着它。」有天清早索尔说，「会吧？」「我会把它挂回它现在挂的地方。」玛伦说。「那你听它，图的是什么？」「图个安心，知道它还在。」索尔摇摇头：「它会比咱们俩都活得久，也不会想咱们。」「我知道。」「那你比大多数人都明白。」「我至少明白听这件事。」「那不是一回事。」「也差不多。」玛伦说，「对我来说，差不多就够了。」"
status: final
emotion: [calm, serious]

[monologue]
type: monologue
context: "Maren's interior monologue after the ferryman leaves; point of view and first-person rhythm must survive."

<monologue-tide>
source: "I never knew whether the bell was a comfort or a reproach. It rang in the same key as my mother's name, the way the tide writes the same line on the sand and then rubs it out. I wanted to keep the sound, the way a child keeps a stone, but a sound has no pocket to be kept in, and so I keep it in my chest and pretend it does not weigh anything."
target: "我始终分不清，那铃声是安慰，还是责备。它响起的音，和母亲名字的音一样，就像潮水总在沙滩上写同一行字，再把它抹掉。我想留住那声音，像孩子收藏一块石头那样；可声音没有可以收纳它的口袋，于是我把它收进胸腔里，再假装它一点都不重。"
status: final
emotion: [nostalgic, sad]

<monologue-stone>
source: "The stone I kept as a girl is still under the floorboard where I left it, and if the house burned I would not grieve for the stone. But the bell is not kept anywhere; it is only heard, and a heard thing has to be heard again or it was never there at all. I keep going back, then, not to keep the bell, but to keep the hearing of it."
target: "我小时候收藏的那块石头，还在我放它的那块地板下面；就算房子烧了，我也不会为石头难过。可那铃不放在任何地方，它只能被听见；而被听见的东西，得再被听见一次，否则它就从没存在过。所以我一次次回去，不是为了留住那铃，是为了留住听它的那一刻。"
status: final
emotion: [nostalgic, sad]

[description]
type: description
context: "Scene-setting at dusk before the final exchange; establishes light, weather and the wind-bell motif."

<description-dusk>
source: "The harbour light turned the water to hammered brass, and one late gull stood on a piling like a man waiting for a letter. Rain hung offshore in a grey curtain that never quite reached the quay. Somewhere a kettle was coming to the boil, and over it all the tin bell swung in the warm wind and rang a single clear note, as if the evening had been waiting to be struck."
target: "港口的灯把水面照成一块锤打过的黄铜，一只迟归的海鸥停在桩上，像在等一封信的人。雨停在近海，垂成一道灰帘，始终没有落到码头。不知哪家烧着的水快要开了；而在这一切之上，那串锡风铃在暖风里荡着，敲出一声清亮的音，仿佛这黄昏一直在等着被敲响。"
status: final
emotion: [nostalgic, calm]

<description-lamplighter>
source: "The lamplighter worked the length of the quay with his long pole, and each lamp he touched woke as if it had only been waiting to be remembered. When he came abreast of the chandler's shop the tin bell caught the lamplight and threw it across the water, and for a moment the whole harbour seemed to hang from that one small, swinging note."
target: "点灯人举着长竿，从码头这头走到那头；他碰过的每一盏灯都像只是等着被想起，就亮了起来。走到杂货铺门前时，那串锡风铃接住了灯光，把它抛到水面上去；有那么一瞬，整座港都像是悬在那一小声荡来荡去的清音上。"
status: final
emotion: [nostalgic, calm]

<description-rain>
source: "By the time the last light was lit the wind had swung to the north, and the grey curtain offshore began to move. It crossed the bar slowly, a whole wall of weather leaning toward the town, and the first drops struck the quay one by one, each one a small cold hand laid on the stone. The bell rang on in the dark, and the rain answered it."
target: "最后一盏灯点亮时，风已经转到了北边，近海那道灰帘开始动了。它缓缓越过沙洲，一整堵天气斜斜地朝镇子压来；头几滴雨一颗接一颗落在码头上，像一只只冰凉的小手按在石面上。那铃在黑暗里继续响，雨声应和着它。"
status: final
emotion: [nostalgic, calm]

[closing]
type: sentence
context: "The story's final line, spoken over the harbour; the motif resolves and the register stays plain."

<closing-line>
source: "The tide keeps nothing, and forgets nothing."
target: "潮水什么都不留，也什么都不忘。"
status: final
emotion: [calm, serious]
